Members of the ASA's Section on Statistical Consulting established the Pathways to
Promotion Committee in 2021 to provide guidance and support for navigating a
career as a collaborative statistician. In three years of existence, the Committee has
produced seven webinars on relevant topics, each attended by more than one hun
dred participants. Committee members have given four oral presentations, organized
three roundtables, led multiple discussions at ASA meetings and published four
articles. These efforts have inspired, created and facilitated new connections for
collaborative statisticians who feel isolated in their career path. This paper describes
the formation and development of the Committee, reports its impact on the commu
nity of collaborative statisticians and discusses potential future directions.
KEYWORDS
biostatistics, medical statistics, teaching statistics
1 | FORMATION OF AND NEED FOR THE PATHWAYS TO PROMOTION COMMITTEE (P2P COMMITTEE)
The Pathways to Promotion Committee (P2P Committee) was formed in January 2021 to provide guidance and support for navigating a career as
a collaborative statistician.
While literature continues to develop (Devick et al., 2022; Griffith et al., 2022; Pomann et al., 2021; Satagopan & Mazumdar, 2021; Taylor
et al., 2023) prior to the formation of the committee relatively few articles provided guidance for the promotion and development of collaborative
statisticians. Most focused on the technical skills and training for collaborative statisticians (Begg & Vaughan, 2012; Kwasny & Daskalakis, 2012;
Love et al., 2017; Zapf et al., 2019) or concerns for the careers of non-tenured faculty, in general (Caye & De Saxe Zerden, 2014; Fitzmorris
et al., 2016; Howell et al., 2010). Only a few studies considered how these challenges impact attaining promotion or tenure for the collaborative
