Since the P2P Committee's founding, the most requested topics for discussion and webinars include the soft skills needed in our profession.
These skills are generally not formally taught in schools and often require interacting with individuals who have been in the field and have experi
ences to draw upon. Isolated statisticians or units that are newly established are at a disadvantage when it comes to developing these skills
because there is no institutional knowledge that is passed down. To help navigate these challenges, the Committee has covered topics including
managing interpersonal relationships, self-advocating during negotiations, avoiding burnout and working as a team member. All of these ideas
stem from suggestions offered by attendees at previous webinars or discussed openly during a P2P Committee meeting. Further scholarship is
needed in these areas.
