Some topics not adequately discussed in the literature are worthy of future scholarship by the community of collaborative statisticians.
Collaborative statisticians may function as consultants (working on short-term projects with clearly defined deliverables), collaborators (in which a
long-term mutual partnership is fostered) or both (positions that encompass both collaborator and consultant roles). Individuals in these positions
will always have a need to balance these roles and scholarship evaluating the different forms of communication is needed. In contrast to many
professions, collaborative statisticians lack standardized promotion guidelines. In a field that encompasses a broad spectrum of titles, ranks and
positions across diverse sectors, this lack of standardization can result in misaligned promotion criteria. It is crucial to delve into topics such as
authorship, grantsmanship, service, computing, project management, continuing education, scholarship, teaching, leadership, research and men
toring to establish a more comprehensive and cohesive framework for the promotion of statisticians. Promotion guidelines for team science may
be useful in this context (McHale et al., 2019; Meurer et al., 2023), but scholarship specifically for collaborative statisticians is more applicable.
Statisticians frequently leverage soft skills and essential attributes like communication, professionalism, ethics and networking. Research is needed
to evaluate the best practices in a statistics curriculum to introduce these topics and teach the diverse skill set needed to work effectively in a col
laborative environment. The models presented in Griffith et al. (2022) are a good starting point. Other topics essential to collaborative statisticians
that would benefit from additional scholarship include leadership and effective collaboration in multidisciplinary research teams; mentoring and
support for career development; and the soft skills, business acumen and strategic planning required to be an independent consulting statistician.
As the committee moves forward, the focus will be on providing support, creating networking opportunities and nurturing camaraderie, par
ticularly for isolated statisticians who may encounter challenges in building connections, accessing resources and finding mentorship. The individ
uals who make up P2P are dedicated to enhancing professional development for every participant, ensuring inclusivity and valuable connections
through discussions on consulting, collaborating, career advancement, soft skills, leadership, mentorship, outreach and empowerment. We hope
the statistical community will complement our efforts in producing scholarship necessary to advance the interests of the collaborative statistician.
6 | CONCLUSION
The P2P Committee is dedicated to supporting individual collaborative statisticians in the promotion process through creating freely accessible
tools, networking opportunities and educational materials. The P2P Committee boasts a unique and flexible structure of offering webinars, fosters
collaboration with local ASA chapters and reaches a broad community across multiple institutions. Deliberate efforts are made in selecting
webinar speakers who resonate with diverse populations, ensuring rich dialogue with common, challenging and conflicting views. The structure
the Committee has chosen for our work provides opportunities for participants to network in breakout rooms and connect with statisticians, who
may have similar or more diverse backgrounds. These information sessions introduce attendees to influential figures in the field, offering opportu
nities to engage in conversations, pose questions and discuss pertinent issues.
In the past 3 years, P2P has also published manuscripts, written news articles and provided conference presentations and roundtables.
Results have been well received by a diverse audience of faculty, staff, industry and academic. The committee remains responsive to statisticians'
needs by having flexibility in its approach, a broad reach and paying close attention to participant feedback. For the foreseeable future, the P2P
Committee will continue to aid in the advancement of statistician's careers and provide camaraderie for statisticians worldwide, while encouraging
scholarship of topics that can enhance promotion, recognition and professional development. We invite the community to apply our model as an
organizational strategy for advocacy and engagement through webinars and inspiring opportunities for scholarship.
